{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-08-24T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Brooklyn Bridge doesn't just connect Manhattan and Brooklyn—it bridges history, engineering and a few surprising stories too. Opened in 1883 after 14 years of construction, it became the world's first steel-wire suspension bridge, forever changing the way New Yorkers crossed the East River.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BKBridge_EN-CA9847334652_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BKBridge_EN-CA9847334652_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Crossing into history","Title":"Brooklyn Bridge, New York City, United States","Copyright":"© shayes17/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/40.706376,-73.996938/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=40.706376,-73.996938;S9;Brooklyn Bridge, New York City, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260824_BKBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Brooklyn+Bridge&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260824_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260824_BKBridge"},"Ssd":"20260824","Name":"BKBridge","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"9847334652","FullDateString":"Aug 24, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Alaska, some of the world's wildest wildlife spectacles unfold far from cities and roads. At Katmai National Park, brown bears line the river, and when the salmon jump, the show begins. Created in 1918 after the dramatic 1912 Novarupta volcanic eruption, the park protects more than 16,000 square kilometres of wilderness, including active volcanoes, tundra and salmon-rich rivers.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KatmaiBear_EN-CA7184475938_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KatmaiBear_EN-CA7184475938_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Meet Katmai's fishing giants","Title":"Brown bear fishing in river, Katmai National Park, Alaska, United States","Copyright":"© Pal Hermansen/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/58.585845,-154.920897/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=58.585845,-154.920897;S9;Katmai National Park, Alaska, USA&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260823_KatmaiBear\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Katmai+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260823_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260823_KatmaiBear"},"Ssd":"20260823","Name":"KatmaiBear","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"7184475938","FullDateString":"Aug 23, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"That quick glimpse of blue fluttering through a field has a story that begins much earlier, with a tiny caterpillar and a surprising survival trick. The common blue is found across Europe, North Africa and parts of Asia, feeding on flower nectar as an adult. It starts life as a small egg, often placed by a female on a host plant such as bird's-foot trefoil. The real surprise comes during its caterpillar stage, when ants play an unexpected role in its survival. After hatching, the caterpillar feeds on leaves before entering the next stage of its transformation. Along the way, it produces a sugary substance called honeydew that ants feed on. As a way of saying thanks, the ants may protect the caterpillar from predators.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CommonBlue_EN-CA6718491810_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CommonBlue_EN-CA6718491810_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Sky tinted wings","Title":"Common blue butterfly, Devon, England","Copyright":"© Ross Hoddinott/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Despite their delicate appearance, males of common blue butterflies actively chase away rival males—and sometimes even larger insects—from favourable patches of flowers.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260822_CommonBlue\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Common+blue+butterfly&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260822_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260822_CommonBlue"},"Ssd":"20260822","Name":"CommonBlue","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"6718491810","FullDateString":"Aug 22, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"You arrive while the sky is turning blue-grey, hear the first burst of music from the midway and realise the Canadian National Exhibition has opened for another season. The event began in 1879 as the Toronto Industrial Exhibition, designed to bring together farming, industry and new ideas from across Canada. More than a century later, that purpose still survives in the exhibits and demonstrations spread across the grounds.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CanadaNE_EN-CA9090606067_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CanadaNE_EN-CA9090606067_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"One last summer spin","Title":"Aerial view of Canadian National Exhibition in Toronto","Copyright":"© Wirestock/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/43.636243,-79.412343/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=43.636243,-79.412343;S9;Exhibition Place, Toronto, Ontario&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260821_CanadaNE\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Canadian+National+Exhibition+2026&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260821_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260821_CanadaNE"},"Ssd":"20260821","Name":"CanadaNE","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"9090606067","FullDateString":"Aug 21, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"An orca breaks the surface of Lynn Canal against the backdrop of the snow-capped Chilkat Mountains in Southeast Alaska. Also known as the killer whale, the orca is the largest member of the dolphin family and one of the ocean's most recognisable predators. Alaska's Inside Passage provides abundant feeding grounds, sustaining salmon runs and a rich variety of marine life that supports these remarkable animals.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LynnCanalOrca_EN-CA6813259779_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LynnCanalOrca_EN-CA6813259779_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Voices of the pod","Title":"An orca surfaces in Lynn Canal near the Chilkat Mountains, Alaska, United States","Copyright":"© John Hyde/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/58.69194,-135.097504/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=58.69194,-135.097504;S9;Lynn Canal, Alaska, USA&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260820_LynnCanalOrca\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Orca+animal&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260820_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260820_LynnCanalOrca"},"Ssd":"20260820","Name":"LynnCanalOrca","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"6813259779","FullDateString":"Aug 20, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The best route here isn't built with concrete. Instead, the tide reveals a rocky path leading from Whytecliff Park to Whyte Islet in West Vancouver. A few hours later, the sea quietly covers the crossing again, making timing part of the experience. This shoreline has drawn visitors for generations. The tide opens the path; wet rocks keep you humble. The reward is a sweeping view back towards the beach and the hillside homes of Gleneagles.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.WhyteCliffP_EN-CA6624264199_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.WhyteCliffP_EN-CA6624264199_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A path between the waves","Title":"Whytecliff Park in West Vancouver, British Columbia","Copyright":"© Aolin Chen/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/0.375514,-123.288861/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=0.375514,-123.288861;S9;Whytecliff Park, West Vancouver, British Columbia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260819_WhyteCliffP\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Whytecliff+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260819_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260819_WhyteCliffP"},"Ssd":"20260819","Name":"WhyteCliffP","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"6624264199","FullDateString":"Aug 19, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From above, Palmanova looks less like a town and more like a carefully drawn star set into the plains of Friuli-Venezia Giulia, Italy. Founded by the Republic of Venice in 1593, this fortress city was designed for defence, order and spectacle. Its streets radiate from a central square, while its walls are shaped into a precise nine-pointed pattern. That geometry was no accident. Palmanova became one of the most influential models of early modern military architecture. It was protected by concentric fortifications built first under Venice and later strengthened and expanded during the Napoleonic period.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Palmanova_EN-CA6466747249_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Palmanova_EN-CA6466747249_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Geometry of a star city","Title":"Aerial view of Palmanova, a fortress city in Friuli, Italy","Copyright":"© Riccardo Saponi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/45.907204,13.311111/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=45.907204,13.311111;S9;Palmanova, Friuli-Venezia Giulia, Italy&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260818_Palmanova\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Palmanova+Italy&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260818_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260818_Palmanova"},"Ssd":"20260818","Name":"Palmanova","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"6466747249","FullDateString":"Aug 18, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Stand in Registan Square and it's easy to see why it is considered the architectural heart of Samarkand—one of Central Asia's oldest cities. This plaza in Uzbekistan is framed by three magnificent madrasas—Islamic centres of learning—whose soaring portals draw the eye upward. Yet some of the square's greatest treasures reveal themselves only when you look closer.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SamarkandCeiling_EN-CA1921310723_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SamarkandCeiling_EN-CA1921310723_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A master class in pattern","Title":"Building detail of Registan Square, Samarkand, Uzbekistan","Copyright":"© Piero M. Bianchi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/39.655009,66.975755/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=39.655009,66.975755;S9;Registan Square, Samarkand, Uzbekistan&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260831_SamarkandCeiling\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Samarkand&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260831_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260831_SamarkandCeiling"},"Ssd":"20260831","Name":"SamarkandCeiling","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"1921310723","FullDateString":"Aug 31, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today, International Whale Shark Day makes room for the world's largest fish. Despite their name, whale sharks are not whales but fish, reaching lengths of up to 18 metres and weighing around 18 metric tonnes. Found in warm tropical seas, they glide through the water with their mouths open, filtering plankton, fish eggs and other tiny prey. This species' distinctive white-spot patterns are unique to each individual, much like human fingerprints.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_EN-CA1504942162_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_EN-CA1504942162_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The fish that outgrew its name","Title":"Whale shark and golden trevally, Cenderawasih Bay, West Papua, Indonesia","Copyright":"© Pete Oxford/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Whale sharks may live for a century or more, giving the world's largest fish an unexpectedly long life span.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Whale+shark&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260830_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark"},"Ssd":"20260830","Name":"YellowShark","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"1504942162","FullDateString":"Aug 30, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Off the coast of Santa Catarina, a state in southern Brazil, the image captures a familiar ritual: surfers waiting beyond the breaking waves, their boards rising and falling with the Atlantic. From above, almost nothing seems to happen. But that's when the real work begins.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SantaCatarina_EN-CA1161995702_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SantaCatarina_EN-CA1161995702_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Reading between the waves","Title":"Aerial view of surfers, Santa Catarina, Brazil","Copyright":"© Wonderful Nature/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-27.374188,-48.654926/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-27.374188,-48.654926;S9;Santa Catarina, Brazil&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260829_SantaCatarina\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Brazil+Santa+Catarina&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260829_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260829_SantaCatarina"},"Ssd":"20260829","Name":"SantaCatarina","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"1161995702","FullDateString":"Aug 29, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At sunset, Mont-Saint Michel rises from the waters of Normandy, France, like a fortress shaped by the sea. Perched on a rocky tidal island, the abbey and village stand at the centre of one of Europe's most dramatic coastal settings. Twice a day, the sea retreats to reveal vast stretches of sand before surging back to reclaim the landscape. At high tide, the mount becomes an island once again. For centuries, travellers timed their journeys to this rhythm, crossing the flats when conditions allowed and watching the sea return hours later.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MichelSunset_EN-CA0604318625_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MichelSunset_EN-CA0604318625_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where tides shape a legend","Title":"Mont-Saint-Michel during high tide, Manche, Normandy, France","Copyright":"© Clement LEONARD/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.637417,-1.5112/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.637417,-1.5112;S9;Mont-Saint-Michel, Normandy, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260828_MichelSunset\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Mont+Saint+Michel&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260828_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260828_MichelSunset"},"Ssd":"20260828","Name":"MichelSunset","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"0604318625","FullDateString":"Aug 28, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Imagine a world without the natural wonders that contain about 90% of Earth's surface freshwater. Lakes provide drinking water, support wildlife, help regulate climate and sustain communities around the globe. In recognition of their vital role, the United Nations designated 27 August as World Lake Day, first observed in 2025. The observance has particular relevance for Canadians, as Canada is home to more than two million lakes that shape its landscapes, ecosystems, recreation and freshwater resources. Protecting them is increasingly important as pollution, overuse and climate change put pressure on many lake environments.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeMagadi_EN-CA0091651040_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeMagadi_EN-CA0091651040_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Water, wildlife and wonder","Title":"Lesser flamingo flock at sunrise, Lake Magadi, Kenya","Copyright":"© Denis-Huot/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-1.902409,36.265224/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-1.902409,36.265224;S9;Lake Magadi, Kenya&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260827_LakeMagadi\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Lake+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260827_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260827_LakeMagadi"},"Ssd":"20260827","Name":"LakeMagadi","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"0091651040","FullDateString":"Aug 27, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As darker nights return to Iceland, visitors will soon look to the skies for a chance to see the aurora borealis. Better known as the northern lights, this luminous phenomenon occurs when particles from the sun interact with gases high in Earth's atmosphere, creating shimmering ribbons of green, pink, purple and sometimes red light. Iceland's northern location and increasingly dark autumn and winter nights make it one of the world's premier destinations for aurora viewing.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AurorasIceland_EN-CA9381288782_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AurorasIceland_EN-CA9381288782_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A sky alive with colour","Title":"Auroras over Kirkjufell, Iceland","Copyright":"© Cavan Images/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/64.939949,-23.307478/3?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=64.939949,-23.307478;S9;Kirkjufell, Iceland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260826_AurorasIceland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Aurora+borealis&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260826_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260826_AurorasIceland"},"Ssd":"20260826","Name":"AurorasIceland","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"9381288782","FullDateString":"Aug 26, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As morning breaks over Elliston, a small seabird appears with a wild iris held across its bill. The scene looks almost like a gift, yet biologists say Atlantic puffins are not known to offer flowers to their mates during courtship. The colourful bill, which becomes brightest in the breeding season and fades later in the year, helps make the photograph memorable. Even their feet turn brighter.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PurplePuffin_EN-CA8959604660_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PurplePuffin_EN-CA8959604660_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable